    "body": "<div class=\"home-page\">\n\n    <!-- The loop behind everything. The footage is still intro.mp4's; what changed is that it is no longer the\n         37 MB 1080p master. It is served as `/assets/intro-web.mp4` — the same 29 seconds at 1280×720, 3.2 MB —\n         because a landing page a stranger opens on a train should not be the heaviest thing on the site. The 10\n         Mbps original stays where it is for `/hub`, which is behind the password and plays it large.\n\n         One file for every screen: `/assets/intro-web.mp4`, which is the 29 seconds of\n         `/assets/intro.mp4` re-encoded to 1280x720 and 3.2 MB. The 35 MB 1080p master stays on disk for\n         `/hub`, which is behind the password and plays it large.\n\n         This used to be a four-rung ladder — a 1080p cut and two fallbacks for wide viewports, a 495 KB\n         cut for phones — with the choice expressed in `media` attributes on each source. There is one\n         source now because a phone and a desktop showing different footage is worse than a phone paying\n         3.2 MB, and the money that buys is better spent on the file being right than on being small.\n         Phones used to load no video at all here; that rule is gone from `home.css`.\n\n         `prefers-reduced-motion` still skips it entirely, on any screen. That is a different question from\n         this one and it outranks this one. -->\n    <video class=\"home-video\" autoplay loop muted playsinline preload=\"metadata\" poster=\"/assets/images/menu-background.webp\">\n        <source src=\"/assets/intro-web.mp4\" type=\"video/mp4\">\n    </video>\n\n    <!-- Three layers, and the scrim is opaque on purpose: this page is a terminal readout, so the painting is a\n         texture behind glass rather than a scene. The wash dims the art, one soft pool of phosphor sits behind the\n         column, and the scanline is the 3px period that does not moire at 1x. The gold wordmark and the Cinzel\n         face it replaced are gone with it; see home.css. -->\n    <div class=\"home-scrim\"></div>\n\n    <main class=\"home-center\">\n        <!-- `sword-crest.png` is drawn at 46px and is a 144px cut of the same art (27 KB against the panel\n             icon's 167 KB, which every button on the site also loads at 32px). -->\n        <img class=\"home-crest\" src=\"/assets/ui/sword-crest.png\" alt=\"\">\n\n        <h1 class=\"home-title\">Dungeon Knights</h1>\n        <p class=\"home-sub\">Coming soon to Robinhood Chain</p>\n\n        <p class=\"home-line\">\n            Recruit knights, clear five themed dungeons, and earn $DNG. The game is in private build.\n            The Points Program is open today, and the 1,024 Genesis Knights are next.\n        </p>\n\n        <div class=\"home-actions\">\n            <a class=\"home-btn home-btn-primary\" href=\"/points\">Join the Points Program</a>\n            <a class=\"home-btn home-btn-secondary\" href=\"/genesis\">Join the Genesis Waitlist</a>\n        </div>\n\n        <!-- The form used to live here, opened by the button that is now a link. It moved to `/genesis` with the\n             rest of the collection — the page that argues for owning one is the page that should ask for an address,\n             and a public landing page keeping a second copy of the same form is two things to keep in step. This page\n             prints no queue size: the owner asked that no running total sit on a public page, and the list itself\n             still lives in the store, where the waitlist tool reads it. -->\n    </main>\n\n    <footer class=\"home-footer\">\n        <span>&copy; 2026 Dungeon Knights. All rights reserved.</span>\n        <a href=\"https://x.com/DNGrobinhood\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Follow @DNGrobinhood</a>\n    </footer>\n</div>",
